WEBVTT

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.980
<b>September, Unified Year 1925</b>

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.980
<b>Imperial Capital Berun, Imperial Strategic Headquarters</b>

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.990
<b>Strategy and Operations
Colonel Erich von Rerugen</b>

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.930
I'm a little tired of this.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:26.580
<b>Military Railways
Captain Maximilian Johann von Uger</b>

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:26.580
The railway folks feel the same way.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.580
Every day, the same food. 
And not good food, at that.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.110
The quality of food has a 
direct effect on morale.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.430
In other circumstances, I'd be asking the 
cooks to exercise their creativity...

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.850
But we can't ask for luxuries.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.950
The front lines, particularly on the 
southern front, are probably far worse.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.800
The southern front?

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.930
The 203rd Aerial Mage 
Battalion is there, too?

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:59.060
I suppose I can make a suggestion 
to General von Zettour.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.580
What do you mean, specifically?

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:07.160
Our nominal allies in Ildoa have been making 
noises about wanting a closer relationship.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.660
If we drop hints about wanting to share
 provisions, they might be willing to provide.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:17.690
I'm sure the 203rd will love it.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.930
<b>Interstitial Episode
 Operation Desert Pasta</b>

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.940
<b>Southern Front, Imperial Military Temporary Base</b>

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.940
<b>Base Command</b>

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.330
I've already drunk half 
my ration for the day.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.330
<b>203rd Aerial Mage Battalion Commander
Major Tanya von Degurechaff</b>

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:46.120
<b>1st Company, Adjutant
First Lieutenant Viktoriya Ivanovna Serebryakov</b>

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:47.640
It hurts not having enough water,
 doesn't it, Major?

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:52.410
Major Degurechaff? Are you there,
 Major Degurechaff?

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.670
What is it, Captain Weiss?

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.300
<b>Vice Commander and 2nd Company Commander
Captain Matheus Johann Weiss</b>

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.300
Splendid news, Major!

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.510
Supplies from home!

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:03.800
Look at the size of those crates!

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.580
Let us through.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.010
Oh, Major!

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.840
Look at this!

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.360
That's pasta!

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.270
Are all these crates filled with pasta?

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.410
Yes.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.150
"We realized it was possible to 
transport dried short pasta by air.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:26.670
The troops who've received it love it.
 I hope you'll enjoy it."

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.170
So the enclosed message says.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.110
I've gotten so sick of that k-brot bread!

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:37.310
We wouldn't want to refuse HQ's kindness.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.170
<b>3rd Company Commander
First Lieutenant Wilibald Koenig</b>

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:38.950
Let's chow down!

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.260
<b>2nd Company
First Lieutenant Warren Grantz</b>

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.420
I'll do the cooking!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.430
<b>4th Company Commander
First Lieutenant Rhiner Neumann</b>

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.380
Men...

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.240
Where do you think we are?

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.200
Desert battles are harsh.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.580
Weapons. Ammo. Parts. Fuel.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:55.140
All that, and even water, 
needs to be transported in.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.020
I think the guys at HQ need 
to learn what it's like

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.310
to not have water come out 
when you turn the faucet.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.450
So, did we get any water with this pasta?

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:10.170
No, not really...

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.740
Sheesh. So the Fatherland 
wants us to chew on raw pasta?

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.300
That wasn't in our orders.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:23.430
If we used up all our water cooking pasta,
 it wouldn't even be funny.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.410
It's as edible as a picture of a dumpling, 
or a pie that's floating in the sky.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.560
What?

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.940
Now, let's get back to our mission.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.080
We do force recon and strike 
their supplies, like always.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.440
We'll hit their supply lines 
and see how they react.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.180
Yes, ma'am!

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:57.170
This is 02 to 01.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.870
We've sighted an enemy supply 
depot that looks like our target.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.490
Very well.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:05.170
Follow the plan. The 2nd Company
 will hit from above.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.840
3rd and 4th Companies,
strike from the flanks.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.100
Don't fly into your allies' firing lines.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.440
All units, attack!

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:13.470
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.900
<b>Southern Front Free Republic Supply Depot</b>

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.160
What?

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:22.690
What is it?

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.670
You see something?

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.520
Enemy attack! Enemy attack!

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.870
Imperial Mages!

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.500
Impossible! Where did they come from?

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.780
Hit them back!

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.330
They came out of nowhere!

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:51.720
Enemy mages to the rear.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.520
They're panicking and rushing up here.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.130
Okay. 2nd Company, draw the mages away.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:58.060
Roger!

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.770
Major, detecting EM waves.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.660
That's the comms facility!

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:07.840
Okay. We've got a present 
from the Empire for it.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:25.290
This is the 4th Company. We see what looks 
like an ammo storage facility.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.290
You should be able to see it 
directly ahead of the 3rd Company!

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:29.990
You guys can hit it, right, 3rd Company?

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.150
Right!

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:39.830
Thanks for gathering it 
all in one place for us!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.950
What happened?

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.270
The ammo dump's on fire!

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.580
This place is finished!

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.360
Retreat! Retreat!

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.830
Get to the evac bunkers!

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.090
Leave the trucks! They're easy targets!

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.470
Okay, we're done here.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.020
No enemy reinforcements.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:27.870
Pretty good work, for a force recon mission.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.860
Major, over here!

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:37.160
Did you find something, 
Lieutenant Serebryakov?

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.590
Look, Major!

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.280
It's filled with 20-liter water tanks!

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:45.150
We shouldn't lack for water for a while now!

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:48.820
Hmm! Just what we were waiting for.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.320
Here you are, Major.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:59.520
Thank you.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.520
Hot, hot, hot, hot...

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.320
Good. It's al dente.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.030
How long has it been since I've had pasta?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.760
This water is so good!

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.330
I never thought I'd get pasta in the desert!

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:11.920
Good job, HQ!

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.720
This is, well...

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.500
It's nice and toothsome, but...

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.070
Depressingly flavorless.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:29.610
It's nice to be able to enjoy the 
original flavor of the ingredients.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:32.880
You can eat it in the ancient Ildoan style 
and not get your hands dirty.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.620
This wasn't what I was hoping for.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.760
But it fills you up, at least.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.550
It's not great.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:43.280
It's not that different than k-brot.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.560
<i>Before all this, I could 
eat whatever I wanted.</i>

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:50.360
<i>Honestly, this is...</i>

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.060
You don't like it either, Major?

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:59.400
Pasta's only good if you 
have sauce and spices to go with it.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.420
<b>Southern Front Imperial Army Temporary Base Command</b>

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:14.920
I propose an Allied Kingdom 
Forward Base as our next target.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.230
We have limited information about them,

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:21.220
but what we have suggests they're moving 
large amounts of supplies at night.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:23.970
We should see what they're stocking up on.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:32.790
Major, I suggest we strike 
the Escargots, not the Limeys.

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:37.640
I'm not a gourmand by any means, 
but there are things even I can't eat.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.710
What about this supply dump?

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:44.340
Given its location, it should 
have some yummy ingredients...

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:55.620
No, I mean...

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.630
I-I-It has important-looking 
supplies, and, um...

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:01.660
It's a good place to test 
the enemy's response.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:10.970
I see. If we hit this place, then we...

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:15.150
We'll go with Lieutenant 
Serebryakov's suggestion.

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:20.130
I'm honored!

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.610
Well done, Lieutenant Serebryakov.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.110
You've got a good nose.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:25.380
Yup.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:31.000
Of course, the goal of the 
operation is still force recon.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.100
But since we're exercising 
some local command discretion,

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:37.020
contact the Southern Front Commander,
 General Romel.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.000
Ma'am!

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.280
Dismissed.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:45.260
<i>It's always best to keep the brass informed.</i>

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:51.100
<i>I've got to make sure to cover 
my ass, bureaucracy-wise.</i>

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:55.440
Um, Major?

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:58.950
What should I name the operation 
when I put it in my report?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:02.070
We're fixing HQ's screw-up. 
Just make something up...

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.630
No.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.380
I just thought of a good name.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.970
Attention!

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:27.540
Men, the cooks at Strategic Command 
have no idea how food works.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:32.320
Thus, we're forced to find 
our own water in the desert,

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:35.360
as well as our own meals!

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:39.270
However, there's no need 
to take any big risks.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:44.510
It would be the height of stupidity 
to lose talented, veteran mages

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.340
for the sake of some flavor.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:51.160
Major, are we more important 
to you than food?

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.890
Correct, Lt. Grantz.

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:58.510
Both you and the food are 
the property of the Empire.

00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:01.080
But you'll rot slower.

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:02.830
I'm honored to hear it, ma'am!

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.440
We always get the worst jobs.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.680
Cause we're the hardest workers.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:15.330
Both of you, that's not quite right.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:18.980
When I give you the shittiest jobs,
 it's 'cause I care.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.950
Okay, time to get to work!

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.170
Just like we always do!

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:32.010
Regardless, what we need is 
always far away from us.

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:36.290
To get it, we must keep working.

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:37.950
And so I now initiate...

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:42.310
"Operation Desert Pasta."

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.800
<b>Southern Front Free Republic Base</b>

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.560
<b>Free Republic Army
General Pierre Michelaud De Lugo</b>

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.550
What's going on?

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:53.560
<b>Free Republic Army
Lt. Colonel Severin Bientot</b>

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:53.570
The Empire knows the status of our supplies.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:12:00.120
Major, I found tomato sauce!

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.560
It has chicken in it!

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:07.110
The attacks look sporadic and random, but...

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:12.460
If you look at which countries 
jurisdictions were attacked,

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:15.540
it reveals a startling 
and dangerous truth.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.050
Got some basil!

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.160
And dried parsley from Ildoa!

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:23.080
Oregano, too!

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:25.420
That'll be good in a tomato-based sauce!

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:29.040
They're not just idiots who 
are after our canned goods.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.430
It's a cunningly-disguised strategy.

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:34.550
Every base that was attacked

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:38.350
was right on the border of another 
country's operational jurisdiction.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.380
Which makes life harder.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:46.620
Those disgusting dogs have already sniffed 
out the weakness in our alliance.

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:50.670
Wine!

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:52.130
And cheese, too!

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:54.340
That's perfect for the pasta!

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:56.340
I could use some side dishes.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.250
I wanna make potato salad.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.250
According to an intercepted 
enemy transmission...

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:05.600
They're calling this mission 
"Operation Desert Pasta"?

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:09.180
The bastards are mocking us!

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:16.210
Everyone...

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.850
Mission complete!

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:21.350
Hooray!

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:31.990
It's so good...

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.000
This chicken is great.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.000
So's the potato salad.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.310
It goes great with the wine!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.250
<i>We're eating better than they do back home!</i>

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:43.910
This is so good!

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:46.590
When's the last time we 
had something so good?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.200
It's amazing!

00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:02.300
<i>It's just a temporary coincidence that 
we're able to eat so well in the desert.</i>

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:09.640
<i>But that coincidence has restored life 
and humanity to the troops of this unit.</i>

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:11.730
<i>It's wonderful.</i>

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.930
May I sit here?

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:16.830
Go ahead.

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:22.030
This is a nice change of pace, huh, Major?

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:23.920
Yeah.

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:26.770
Food is important.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:15.490
<b>Imperial Capital Berun, Imperial Air Force Base</b>

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:20.490
I didn't expect such splendid results.

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:26.130
It was hard to get another shipment,

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:30.460
but the guys at the front are 
working so hard, I just had to.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.340
Bring on the pasta!

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.190
We're sending more to the southern front!

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:36.020
Sir!

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:37.750
Keep the noodles coming!

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:39.130
Hurry, hurry!
